<sect1 id="UdpDelaySimRunner_8h_1DESCRIPTION">
<title>DESCRIPTION</title>
<para>This <ref refid="classCpuFlagDetection" kindref="compound">CpuFlagDetection</ref> class file is used for detecting the current processor&apos;s CPU flags to determine which CPU instructions are supported. It is cross platform. It is used by this project&apos;s CMake build system when compiling locally (not cross-compiling) to determine if any hardware accelerated functions should be compiled in. For more information, see the example from <ulink url="https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/cpp/intrinsics/cpuid-cpuidex?view=msvc-170">https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/cpp/intrinsics/cpuid-cpuidex?view=msvc-170</ulink> which this code is based on. Also see <ulink url="https://www.boost.org/doc/libs/master/boost/beast/core/detail/cpu_info.hpp">https://www.boost.org/doc/libs/master/boost/beast/core/detail/cpu_info.hpp</ulink> from which the cross platform code idea is based on. </para>
</sect1>
